cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Aeolus.jl: a Julia-native large-eddy simulation framework"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dulny"
    given-names: "Andrzej"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/badulion/Aeolus.jl"
abstract: >-
  Aeolus.jl is a large-eddy simulation framework written in Julia, with a
  staggered finite-volume dynamical core behind an AbstractMesh interface,
  a high-fidelity radiation stack (correlated-k gas optics, two-stream and
  3-D Monte-Carlo transfer, urban radiosity, spectral BRDF surface optics),
  and exact moist thermodynamics with bulk and Lagrangian microphysics. Its
  flagship application is urban climate: simulating how a real city, built
  from OpenStreetMap geometry, heats and cools over a diurnal cycle.
keywords:
  - large-eddy simulation
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - atmospheric boundary layer
  - urban climate
  - urban heat island
  - radiative transfer
  - Julia
license: MIT
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
